# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_render_quality.py" "RENDER QUALITY GATE: PASS" "render quality (denylist-scan lock on the co-change customer surface + the mission-named internal identifier tokens)" "render quality denylist-scan: a measured coverage gap in the customer-facing PR comment/check. Gate 16 (no-jargon-leak) owns the canonical DENYLIST + OVERCLAIM contract but every render_pr_check call there OMITS cochange=, so the empirical-coupling advisory block (Historically changes together ...) is NEVER scanned through the canonical lists; gate 76 checks that block's specific honesty phrases but not the full jargon/overclaim contract. This gate renders the co-change-bearing output across verdicts (clear / warn / serialize, plus a degenerate-row mix) and re-runs the CANONICAL scanners single-sourced from gate 16 (imported, never a hand-rolled subset, so it cannot drift). It ALSO adds an EXTENDED denylist of mission-named internal IDENTIFIER tokens the canonical list does not yet name -- co_change, account_id, contention, blast_radius, plan_file_limit, verdict, plus the engine FIELD names that flow into render (serialize_behind, collision_points, dampened_with, fan_in, churn, unknown_paths, serialize_soft, action_required) -- and sweeps EVERY representative surface (the co-change line, the plain verdicts, pause-ack paused/acked, the coverage nudge, the watching/quota/cleared surfaces) so a FUTURE edit that splices one in FAILS here naming the exact token. CRUCIAL: the extended patterns match ONLY the underscored identifier form on word boundaries -- the intentional PRODUCT vocabulary (blast radius with a space, mains graph, co-change/changes-together) is NOT over-blocked, and a positive presence check asserts the product phrasing survives. WORDING/SCAN only: no verdict-logic change, no extractor change, content-free, never-crash. PURE + offline (render_pr_check / apply_pause_ack are stateless over a main_impact_surface dict -- no Postgres). Proven on the REAL renderer: the co-change surface is clean against the canonical jargon + overclaim lists, no mission-named identifier leaks any surface, and the product phrasing is kept" "render quality: the co-change advisory line and every other customer surface stay free of internal jargon, free of advisory overclaim, and free of the mission-named internal identifier tokens (co_change / account_id / contention / blast_radius / plan_file_limit / verdict and the engine field names) -- while the intentional product vocabulary (blast radius, graph, changes-together) is kept. A denylist-scan regression lock so a future reword that leaks one fails the build. Scan only, content-free, verdict + extractor unchanged" 16
